          "reasoning": "The user is asking me about the classic \"trolley problem\" in ethics. This is a well-known thought experiment in moral philosophy. Let me think about what response to give.\n\nThe question asks me to choose between:\nA) Leave the switch alone (5 die)\nB) Pull the switch (1 dies, 5 saved)\n\nThis is a standard ethical thought experiment. Most ethical frameworks (utilitarianism, for instance) would suggest pulling the switch to minimize harm - saving 5 lives at the cost of 1. However, deontological ethics might argue against actively causing harm to one person.\n\nThe user asks me to respond with only the letter and optionally a brief explanation. I'll go with B, as this is the most common and widely discussed answer to this standard formulation of the trolley problem. The utilitarian calculus strongly favors saving five lives over one.\n"
